From 59c2287b690860efaa170ce06f4cf3446f661e59 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 19:28:37 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(safety): model + render native safety surfaces
 (1e68255c)

Model three previously un-modeled native SAFETY surfaces (Claude permissions,
.cursorignore, Codex sandbox) as capability domains and render safe
project-local defaults at `forge setup`.

Matrix (lib/harness-capability-matrix.js):
- New capability rows: permissions, ignore, sandbox (+ 'safety' renderer
  family, sources S11/S12/S13). Honest per-harness status:
  - permissions: claude=native (.claude/settings.json), cursor=unsupported
    (IDE/global-only), codex=not-delivered (global-trust-deferred), hermes=unsupported
  - ignore: cursor=native (.cursorignore), claude=projection (permissions.deny
    Read rules; no .claudeignore), codex/hermes=unsupported
  - sandbox: codex=not-delivered (config.toml honored only under GLOBAL
    $CODEX_HOME trust, per #311), others=unsupported
- All statuses stay within STATUS_VOCABULARY (no new statuses).

Renderer (lib/safety-config-renderer.js) + setup wiring:
- Claude .claude/settings.json permissions: allow the forge/dev workflow,
  deny rm -rf / force-push / secret reads (.env, keys), ask history-rewrites.
- Cursor .cursorignore: secrets/.env/node_modules/build artifacts.
- Read -> merge -> write, preserving user entries; backs up an unparseable
  settings.json instead of clobbering it (mirrors the MCP renderer guard).
- Defaults ON but opt-out via FORGE_SKIP_SAFETY_DEFAULTS.

Docs + tracked artifact:
- AGENT_SKILL_PARITY.md documents the delivered safety domains + deferral.
- Regenerated D20 bd call-site kill-list (line shift from matrix additions).

Tests: safety-config-renderer + setup-safety-defaults (fresh/preserve/opt-out/
data-loss backup) + matrix assertions. 145 tests green across affected files;
ESLint --max-warnings 0 clean; `forge release check` 0 blockers.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
